{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1744809,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"WPTC - Wireless Power Transfer","festival_id":504454,"organization_id":675999,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-08-27T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-13T22:20:54+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/wptc-wireless-power-transfer-techfest26-annual-technical-festival-of-sliet-sant-longowal-institute-of-engin-1744809","region":"online","details":"<p><strong>All That You Need To Know About WPTC-Wireless Power Transfer - techFEST'26:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>For Non-SLIET Participants Only:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>techFEST'26 is North India's premier technical festival, organised by Sant Longowal Institute of Engineering and Technology (SLIET), Longowal, Punjab. This is a paid opportunity with the early-bird packages mentioned below.<\/p>\n<p>Register Now: <a href=\"http:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\">www.techfest26.com<\/a><\/p>\n<p>We cordially invite you to WPTC - Wireless Power Transfer, organised as part of techFEST'26 - Annual Technical Festival of SLIET. Showcase your talent, compete with the sharpest minds and earn your moment of glory.<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><strong>About The Event:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Design and build a Wireless Power Transfer (WPT) system using inductive or resonant coupling, capable of powering a standard 5 W load provided by the organizers.<\/p>\n<p>Number of rounds: 1.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Prelims:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Teams qualifying from Round 1 will proceed to the practical challenge. Each team will demonstrate its self-built WPT system using the organizer-provided standard 5 W load.<\/p>\n<p>The system will be tested under controlled conditions for:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Output Power.<\/li>\n<li>Transfer Efficiency.<\/li>\n<li>Transfer Distance.<\/li>\n<li>System Stability.<\/li>\n<li>Safety and Build Quality.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>The transmitter and receiver will initially be aligned and tested at a specified reference distance. The distance between the Tx and Rx coils will then be increased to determine the maximum usable transfer distance at which the system can still deliver the required output.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Scoring And Judging Criteria:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Efficiency: Ratio of output power to input power.<\/li>\n<li>Transfer Distance: Maximum usable distance achieved.<\/li>\n<li>Fixed Distance Power Delivery: Ability to drive the 5 W load reliably at a specified test distance.<\/li>\n<li>Build &amp; Safety: Circuit stability, build quality, and adherence to safety.<\/li>\n<li>Technical Viva: Ability to explain design choices, resonance, tuning, and coupling coefficient.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Website: <a href=\"http:\/\/www.techfest26.com\/\">www.techfest26.com<\/a> | Email: <a href=\"mailto:techfest@sliet.ac.in\">techfest@sliet.ac.in<\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>Rules And Regulations - General Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>All participants must carry a valid college ID card and their techFEST'26 registration receipt.<\/li>\n<li>Reporting time will be communicated to registered teams; late reporting may lead to walkover.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the judges and organisers will be final and binding in all matters.<\/li>\n<li>Any form of misconduct, plagiarism or use of unfair means leads to immediate disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Participants are responsible for their own equipment and personal belongings.<\/li>\n<li>Organisers reserve the right to modify any rule at any time; updates are announced at the venue.<\/li>\n<li>Individual event; components and breadboards provided.<\/li>\n<li>Datasheets are available on request.<\/li>\n<li>Burning components is allowed twice per round - the third smoke ends your battle.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to students of all institutes and all degree programmes (unless specified otherwise in the event rules above).<\/li>\n<li>Participants must be registered for techFEST'26 through the official portal.<\/li>\n<li>Cross-college teams are welcome.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Prizes:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Prizes worth Rs 45,000+ for this event.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>1st place: Winner trophy\/certificate and cash prize.<\/li>\n<li>2nd place: Runner-up certificate and cash prize.<\/li>\n<li>3rd place: Certificate and cash prize.<\/li>\n<li>Certificates of participation for all registered participants.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Why You Should Participate:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>WPTC is more than a competition - it is a platform to test your skills against the brightest minds from institutes across the region, learn from judges and mentors, and build memories that last far beyond the festival. Winners take home cash prizes, trophies and certificates that strengthen their resumes, while every participant leaves with experience, exposure and connections. Whether you are a seasoned competitor or a first-timer, the arena at techFEST'26 welcomes you.<\/p>\n<p><strong>About The Festival - techFEST'26 At SLIET:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>techFEST'26 is the annual technical festival of Sant Longowal Institute of Engineering and Technology (SLIET), Longowal, Punjab - a deemed-to-be university under the Ministry of Education, Government of India. Established in 1989, accredited with Grade A by NAAC, SLIET spreads across a lush 451-acre campus with 11 departments and more than 5,000 students. With a legacy of over 28 years, techFEST'26 - themed 'Technology and Sciences for Sustainable Earth' - features 50+ events across 11 clubs and a total prize pool of Rs 5,00,000+, along with workshops, exhibitions, guest lectures and a grand cultural evening.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Festival Highlights At techFEST'26:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>50+ technical, non-technical and cultural events across 11 clubs.<\/li>\n<li>Total prize pool worth Rs 5,00,000+.<\/li>\n<li>Grand cultural evening and pro-shows.<\/li>\n<li>Hands-on workshops, exhibitions and expert guest lectures.<\/li>\n<li>Early-bird registration packages for participants from all institutes.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><em><strong>Accommodation And Meals:<\/strong><\/em><\/p>\n<p><strong>Select Your Registration Package<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Registration for the techFEST&rsquo;26 package is compulsory for accommodation and other perks, while participation in individual events is free*.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Note:<\/strong> Registration is mandatory for participation. Fee once paid is non-refundable.<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":27463276,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-08-27T02:02:36+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-06T22:20:54+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"VZz7xCD","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":0,"show_reviews_only_user":0,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":54,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-08-27 12:17:53","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participation_certificate":true,"closed_at":null,"linkedInEventId":"","teams":[],"players":[],"logoUrl":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/images\/75x75\/uploadedManual-6aad5056a134f_logo.webp","logoUrl2":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/images\/150x150\/uploadedManual-6aad5056a134f_logo.webp","regnRequirements":{"id":2476115,"opportunity_id":1744809,"festival_id":null,"max_team_size":3,"min_team_size":1,"start_regn_dt":"2026-